    "H3_interpretation": "The preregistered expectation that explicit calibration was necessary was false. A two-field assay signature robustly separates climate target classes across both admitted assay-process worlds without identifying or calibrating the assay world itself."
  },
  "main_findings": [
    "Repeating the same deterministic systematically biased assay twice changed robust target-pair coverage in 0 scored field-by-fiber audits.",
    "Explicit assay-process calibration was genuinely necessary for some future-target fibers: 2 climate fibers, 2 biotic-stress fibers and 3 barrier-restoration fibers had no robust assay-only solution but became solvable with calibration.",
    "The complete calibrated action library resolved every one of the 67 future-target-unresolved W1 fibers.",
    "H3 was refuted: the S11 dormant-climate fiber did not require explicit calibration. The exact robust minimum was A_level plus antagonist_excluded, size 2, both with and without the calibration action available.",
    "Multiple assay channels can therefore provide implicit target-level self-calibration: their joint observed signature can separate target classes across observation worlds even when no single assay is robust and the observation-process identity itself remains unresolved.",
    "Calibration can still be useful even when not strictly necessary for solvability: in the frozen biotic-stress panel it appeared in four canonical robust minima although only two fibers were assay-only impossible."
  ],
  "claim_boundary": [
    "The systematically_miscalibrated observation world is a synthetic deterministic coding-bias fixture, not a calibrated laboratory error model.",
    "The self-calibration result concerns target separation under a fixed finite observation-world universe; it does not imply that two assays estimate real-world bias parameters.",
    "Repeated-assay equivalence applies to repeated deterministic measurements under the same systematic observation world, not independent random error.",
    "Action count is a combinatorial information count, not monetary, logistical, temporal or ethical field cost.",
    "Canonical assay frequency is not a causal-importance ranking.",
    "The result does not alter Phase-I through Phase-VI, EOG-WF, or the frozen first BAM inverse-identifiability paper."
  ]
